Make webviews work in a single-origin static build.

Two independent causes, both silent, both fatal to every webview (markdown
preview, notebooks, the settings UI):

1. The host page proves it is on a dedicated per-webview origin by checking that
   location.hostname equals a sha-256 of the parent origin. A static folder has
   exactly one origin, so that can never hold. Accept the explicit same-origin
   case instead.

   Deliberate trade-off: webview content is then not isolated from workbench
   storage (localStorage, IndexedDB, OPFS). Cross-origin deployments keep full
   validation.

2. Service worker script requests bypass service workers (the request carries
   serviceWorkers:'none'), so a worker living only inside a RuntimeFS virtual
   folder 404s and never registers. Register it from the real RuntimeFS host
   root, and pass the webview directory as both an explicit narrower scope and
   an explicit vscode-resource-root the worker reads back.

Patching the inline script invalidates the sha-256 the page's own CSP pins for
it, and the browser then blocks the script with no console entry. staticify.mjs
recomputes that hash on every build.
